Negative control for the DRIVE-MEMBERS-COME-FROM-THE-PORT law (`R6-29`).

Saves through the flow machine's member on every module, so an editor backed by
the shared data manager — which saves through `update` — fires nothing at all.
The declaration channel stays deleted; what is withdrawn is the surface reading
which pair the live port actually publishes, which is the whole reason the
channel could go.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the form-flow surface spec — a manager-backed editor's Save calls the
member that module publishes, and the settled save closes the editor.

